Subject: [PATCH 6/9] Rebuild proxies the PostProject sidecar reports as stale

Kdenlive checks a proxied clip's hash only when its proxy is missing,
so a replaced source keeps playing its old proxy. When a project
opens, ask the sidecar about each proxy whose clip it knows. A source
whose content no longer matches the sidecar is observed first, and a
proxy that PostProject then evaluates as stale is offered for
rebuilding in the relink dialog. The clip is hashed again, so the new
proxy gets a name of its own.

diff --git a/src/doc/documentchecker.cpp b/src/doc/documentchecker.cpp
index 956ffc16b..3dfccb7d2 100644
--- a/src/doc/documentchecker.cpp
+++ b/src/doc/documentchecker.cpp
@@ -1115,6 +1115,17 @@ QString DocumentChecker::getMissingProducers(QDomElement &e, const QDomNodeList
             item.originalFilePath = proxy;
             item.type = MissingType::Proxy;
             m_items.push_back(item);
+#ifdef HAVE_POSTPROJECT
+        } else if (!slideshow &&
+                   PostProjectSidecar::isProxyStale(m_url.toLocalFile(), Xml::getXmlProperty(e, QStringLiteral("kdenlive:control_uuid")), original, proxy)) {
+            // The proxy was made from content the clip no longer has. Rebuild it,
+            // and hash the clip again so the new proxy gets a name of its own.
+            Xml::removeXmlProperty(e, QStringLiteral("kdenlive:file_hash"));
+            item.originalFilePath = proxy;
+            item.type = MissingType::Proxy;
+            item.status = MissingStatus::Reload;
+            m_items.push_back(item);
+#endif
         }
         return resource;
     }
